# Citation metadata for vibey. GitHub renders this as "Cite this repository" on the
# repository page; citation managers (Zotero, Zenodo, ...) read it directly.
# Format: Citation File Format 1.2.0 — https://citation-file-format.github.io/
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use vibey, or build on its design, please cite the research paper listed under
  preferred-citation, and cite this repository for the software itself.
title: vibey
type: software
abstract: >-
  A queue-based, six-phase conductor for autonomous software delivery on top of the
  *loop autonomous session runners: spec interview, design, build, review, and opt-in
  deployment, with an append-only PostgreSQL ledger and a lossless engine handoff.
authors:
  - family-names: Steinberger
    given-names: Adam Matthew
    website: https://vibewithadam.matthewsteinberger.com/
license: MIT
version: 2.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-18"
repository-code: https://github.com/the-vibey-project/vibey
url: https://the-vibey-project.github.io/vibey/main/
keywords:
  - autonomous software delivery
  - coding agents
  - orchestration
  - event-sourced ledger
  - PostgreSQL
  - engine rotation
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: >-
    Ledger-Mediated Orchestration: Vendor-Independent Autonomous Software Delivery over
    a Pool of Coding Agents
  authors:
    - family-names: Steinberger
      given-names: Adam Matthew
  year: 2026
  url: https://the-vibey-project.github.io/vibey/main/paper.pdf
  notes: >-
    Published on the project's documentation site as a journal-formatted PDF
    (https://the-vibey-project.github.io/vibey/main/paper.pdf) and as HTML
    (https://the-vibey-project.github.io/vibey/main/paper/). The Markdown source is
    docs/paper.md in the repository. No DOI or preprint identifier has been assigned yet.
references:
  - type: book
    title: "vibey — The Documentation"
    authors:
      - family-names: Steinberger
        given-names: Adam Matthew
    year: 2026
    url: https://the-vibey-project.github.io/vibey/main/book.pdf
    notes: >-
      The complete documentation exported as a book: EPUB at
      https://the-vibey-project.github.io/vibey/main/book.epub, print-ready PDF at
      https://the-vibey-project.github.io/vibey/main/book.pdf, and print HTML at
      https://the-vibey-project.github.io/vibey/main/book-print.html.
